 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Mayo Clinic LDCT — exploration des données réelles\n",
    "\n",
    "Ce notebook vérifie que le pipeline Mayo Clinic (téléchargement idc-index → cache `.npy` →\n",
    "`MayoSliceDataset` → injection dans `get_setup`) fonctionne bien de bout en bout, et montre\n",
    "des exemples visuels à chaque étape :\n",
    "\n",
    "1. aperçu brut de plusieurs coupes Mayo (avant tout traitement tomographique) ;\n",
    "2. distribution des intensités après normalisation `[0, 1]` ;\n",
    "3. comparaison de plusieurs patients côte à côte ;\n",
    "4. injection d'une vraie coupe dans `get_setup` : phantom / sinogramme / rétroprojection\n",
    "   (exactement le même triptyque que dans `running_kkt.ipynb`, mais avec une vraie image\n",
    "   au lieu du phantom TGV synthétique) ;\n",
    "5. effet du niveau de bruit sur le sinogramme et la rétroprojection.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Imports & configuration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "device = cuda\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "from data.mayo_dataset import MayoSliceDataset\n",
    "from Algo_setuptorch import Params, get_setup, build_algo_functions\n",
    "\n",
    "device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\n",
    "print('device =', device)\n",
    "\n",
    "SIZE = 512\n",
    "N_ANGLES = 180\n",
    "NOISE = 0.05\n",
    "MAYO_CACHE_DIR = \"./data/mayo_cache_512\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# patients dont le cache .npy a déjà été construit (cf. mayo_dataset.py --build-cache)\n",
    "PATIENTS = [\"L004\", \"L006\", \"L012\", \"L014\", \"L019\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "params = Params(size=SIZE)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Aperçu brut des coupes Mayo\n",
    "\n",
    "Chargement direct via `MayoSliceDataset`, sans passer par `get_setup` — juste pour vérifier\n",
    "que les DICOM ont bien été lus, converties en HU, fenêtrées et normalisées dans `[0, 1]`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "784 coupes chargées au total, sur 5 patients\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1600x360 with 5 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dataset = MayoSliceDataset(PATIENTS, cache_dir=MAYO_CACHE_DIR)\n",
    "print(f\"{len(dataset)} coupes chargées au total, sur {len(PATIENTS)} patients\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# une coupe \"milieu de volume\" par patient (évite les toutes premières/dernières coupes,\n",
    "# souvent moins informatives anatomiquement)\n",
    "offsets = {}\n",
    "idx = 0\n",
    "for p in PATIENTS:\n",
    "    n = sum(1 for pp, _ in dataset.index if pp == p)\n",
    "    offsets[p] = idx + n // 2\n",
    "    idx += n\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, len(PATIENTS), figsize=(3.2 * len(PATIENTS), 3.6))\n",
    "for ax, p in zip(axes, PATIENTS):\n",
    "    img = dataset[offsets[p]][0].numpy()  # (H, W)\n",
    "    ax.imshow(img, cmap='gray', vmin=0, vmax=1)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(p)\n",
    "    ax.axis('off')\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Coupe médiane par patient (Full Dose Images, normalisées [0,1])')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Distribution des intensités après normalisation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 700x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 4))\n",
    "for p in PATIENTS:\n",
    "    img = dataset[offsets[p]][0].numpy().ravel()\n",
    "    ax.hist(img, bins=80, histtype='step', label=p, density=True)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('intensité normalisée [0,1]')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('densité')\n",
    "ax.set_title('Histogramme des intensités (fenêtrage HU [-160, 240])')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Plusieurs coupes du même patient\n",
    "\n",
    "Pour vérifier que le tri par `ImagePositionPatient` donne bien un empilement anatomiquement\n",
    "cohérent (pas de coupes mélangées / dans le désordre)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1800x350 with 6 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "patient = PATIENTS[0]\n",
    "n_patient_slices = sum(1 for pp, _ in dataset.index if pp == patient)\n",
    "sample_idx = np.linspace(0, n_patient_slices - 1, 6).astype(int)\n",
    "base = next(i for i, (pp, _) in enumerate(dataset.index) if pp == patient)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 6, figsize=(18, 3.5))\n",
    "for ax, i in zip(axes, sample_idx):\n",
    "    img = dataset[base + i][0].numpy()\n",
    "    ax.imshow(img, cmap='gray', vmin=0, vmax=1)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'coupe {i}')\n",
    "    ax.axis('off')\n",
    "plt.suptitle(f'Patient {patient} — 6 coupes réparties sur tout le volume')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Injection dans `get_setup` : phantom / sinogramme / rétroprojection\n",
    "\n",
    "On remplace `odl.phantom.tgv_phantom(U)` par une vraie coupe Mayo via le nouveau paramètre\n",
    "`phantom_array`. Même triptyque que dans `running_kkt.ipynb`, mais avec une image réelle."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "setup ready: torch.Size([1, 1, 512, 512]) torch.Size([1, 1, 1000, 1000]) torch.Size([1, 1, 512, 512])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "example_img = dataset[offsets[PATIENTS[0]]][0].numpy()  # (SIZE, SIZE), déjà [0,1]\n",
    "\n",
    "setup = get_setup(\n",
    "    size=SIZE,\n",
    "    n_angles=N_ANGLES,\n",
    "    seed=0,\n",
    "    noise_level=NOISE,\n",
    "    device=device,\n",
    "    phantom_array=example_img,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "phantom = setup['phantom']\n",
    "sino = setup['data']\n",
    "init = setup['initial_state']\n",
    "print('setup ready:', phantom.shape, sino.shape, init.shape)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1400x400 with 3 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(14, 4))\n",
    "ax[0].imshow(phantom[0, 0].cpu(), cmap='gray'); ax[0].set_title(f'Coupe Mayo ({PATIENTS[0]})'); ax[0].axis('off')\n",
    "ax[1].imshow(sino[0, 0].cpu(), cmap='gray', aspect='auto'); ax[1].set_title(r'Sinogramme  $y = K\\,u$'); ax[1].axis('off')\n",
    "ax[2].imshow(init[0, 0].cpu(), cmap='gray'); ax[2].set_title(r'Rétroprojection  $K^\\top y$  (init)'); ax[2].axis('off')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Plusieurs patients dans `get_setup` côte à côte\n",
    "\n",
    "Vérifie que le pipeline complet (chargement → normalisation → projection → bruit) se comporte\n",
    "correctement sur différents patients, pas seulement sur un exemple isolé."
   ]
  },
